# Where this machine is. Copy to /etc/monitoring/location.yaml and edit.
#
# NOT in this repository on purpose. The node files are committed and this
# repository is public, so coordinates in one would be published to anyone who
# reads it. The install script creates the real file; this example stays.
#
# The numbers below are a nearby town rounded to a tenth of a degree, which
# is about ten kilometres of fuzz and under a minute of error in a sunrise.
# So the example gives nothing away and still shows the shape.
#
# Both numbers are needed. Latitude sets how long the day is. Longitude sets
# what time solar noon happens, which is what turns a day length into clock
# times, and this site is about seven degrees off its timezone's central
# meridian: without it every sunrise is half an hour out, which for a window
# built around legal shooting light is the whole feature.
#
# Degrees and decimals, not degrees and minutes. 37 degrees 2 minutes north
# is 37.05, not 37.02. West and south are negative.
latitude: 37.0
longitude: -97.4

# An IANA zone name, not an offset. The schedules have to follow daylight
# saving, and two days a year an offset is an hour wrong.
timezone: America/Chicago
